          "explanation": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><p>$X\\sim\\text{Binomial}(n=18,\\;p=1/6)$ since each roll independently shows a two with probability $1/6$. Then $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=np(1-p)=18\\times\\tfrac16\\times\\tfrac56=\\tfrac{90}{36}=2.5$, so $\\sigma=\\sqrt{2.5}=1.5811\\approx1.581$.</p></div><div class=\"ml-vi\"><p>$X\\sim\\text{Nhị thức}(n=18,\\;p=1/6)$ vì mỗi lần gieo độc lập cho mặt hai chấm với xác suất $1/6$. Khi đó $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=np(1-p)=18\\times\\tfrac16\\times\\tfrac56=2{,}5$, nên $\\sigma=\\sqrt{2{,}5}=1{,}5811\\approx1{,}581$.</p></div>"
